# Nine Dire Blunderbusses on one Ornithopter give it nine instances of "Whenever this creature attacks, you may sacrifice
# an artifact other than Dire Blunderbuss ..." (CR 613.1f), each naming the Blunderbuss that gave it (the layers' giver of
# that instance, CR 113.2c): nine attack triggers, as many as there are Blunderbusses, with no cap on how many one creature
# can tell apart. As each resolves, the Blunderbuss it names may not be sacrificed (the refusals) while every other is
# still offered: the first sacrifices a Gleemox instead (the positive control), and its reflexive ability deals the
# Ornithopter's power, 27 with nine Blunderbusses' +3/+0, to Bot2's Ornithopter; the other eight are declined.
# Setup: each Flail is cast and crafted with a Black Lotus, sacrificed for the mana, as its material from the graveyard;
# Gleemoxen pay the rest, and Wheels of Fortune draw the cards. The script ends with the triggers resolved, before blocks.

